# Run to create (needs the YubiKey master identity):
#   agenix-rekey edit ./dmvault-secrets.age
#
# Contents (KEY=value format) — four keys, NO DATOMIC_URL:
#   DATOMIC_PASSWORD=<alphanumeric only. orcpub embeds this in a datomic: URI,
#                     and non-URL-safe chars (; ! / + # & space) break parsing.
#                     Generate a safe one with `openssl rand -hex 24`.>
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD=<datomic admin password — MUST differ from DATOMIC_PASSWORD>
#   SIGNATURE=<random 20+ char string; symbols are fine (never used in a URI)>
#   EMAIL_SECRET_KEY=<Resend API key, starts with re_>
#
# DATOMIC_URL is intentionally NOT a secret. It lives in dmvault.nix as plain
# code (`datomic:free://datomic:4334/orcpub`), and orcpub appends
# `?password=<DATOMIC_PASSWORD>` at startup. Keeping the URL out of the
# hand-edited secret removes the scheme-prefix / newline / special-char
# footguns that a typed URL is prone to.
